From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:53:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: qrtr: coalesce HELLO senders under the endpoint lock

The restored nameserver reply must precede service announcements, even
when the incoming HELLO wins the race with proactive registration work.
Keep proactive work for peers which wait for the host to initiate, but
send only one HELLO per endpoint session. Takashi Iwai reported that
sending both proactive and reply HELLO packets confuses firmware.

Check hello_sent at the final transmit critical section, after verifying
the endpoint still exists. Consume a coalesced skb and return success;
the existing successful-send path sets hello_sent under the same lock.
Keep the MHI resume reset and delayed retry behavior unchanged.

This coalescing implementation is local, not part of Takashi's patch.
It addresses initial SMD endpoint startup on Polaris, not every MHI reset
race or transport-error announcement retry.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/878q55sfxo.wl-tiwai@suse.de/
Fixes: 544d85de4dc2 ("net: qrtr: Send HELLO message on endpoint register")
---
 net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c b/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
--- a/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c
@@ -384,10 +384,15 @@
 	if (!rc) {
 		mutex_lock(&node->ep_lock);
 		rc = -ENODEV;
-		if (node->ep)
+		if (!node->ep) {
+			kfree_skb(skb);
+		} else if (type == QRTR_TYPE_HELLO && node->hello_sent) {
+			/* Coalesce the NS reply and proactive handshake work. */
+			consume_skb(skb);
+			rc = 0;
+		} else {
 			rc = node->ep->xmit(node->ep, skb);
-		else
-			kfree_skb(skb);
+		}
 		if (!rc && type == QRTR_TYPE_HELLO)
 			node->hello_sent = true;
 		mutex_unlock(&node->ep_lock);
